  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SUPPORTING THE PROTECTION AND RECOVERY OF THE MALAYAN TIGER IN KENYIR-TAMAN NEGARA CORE AREA, PENINSULAR MALAYSIA 3</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO STABILIZE AND INCREASE THE TIGER POPULATION BY 50%, FROM EIGHT TIGERS (2018 SURVEY) TO 12 TIGERS BY 2025, WITH AT LEAST FOUR FEMALE AND TWO MALE TIGERS PERSISTING FOR THREE YEARS OR LONGER. THE PROJECT OBJECTIVES ARE AS FOLLOWS: (1) ANNUALLY UPDATE STATUS OF TIGER AND PREY POPULATIONS IN THE CORE AREA (2) ADDRESS CRITICAL THREATS TO TIGERS IN THE CORE AREA AND (3) DESIGN HIGHLY TARGETED PRACTICAL INTERVENTION MEASURES, SUCH AS COORDINATE A PENINSULA-WIDE THREAT ASSESSMENT TO THE MALAYAN TIGER AND DEVELOP TARGETED INTERVENTION STRATEGIES FOR SPECIFIC PROBLEMS, TO ADDRESS THE MOST PRESSING THREATS TO TIGERS IN PENINSULAR MALAYSIA.</narrative>
  </description>
